DESCRIPTION
-----------
External validation of the best miRNA + clinical prognostic model for
High-Grade Serous Ovarian Cancer (HGSOC), trained on the TCGA-OV cohort.
 
This script loads a pre-trained serialized model (.pkl) and evaluates it on
three external cohorts stratified by treatment type.
 
================================================================================
SAVED MODEL — best_model_auc_v1.pkl
================================================================================
 
The .pkl file is a dictionary with three keys:
 
  KEY               TYPE                      DESCRIPTION
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  "model"           CalibratedClassifierCV    Full fitted pipeline (see below)
  "threshold"       float                     Decision threshold tuned to
                                              maximise balanced accuracy 
  "features"        list[str]                 Names of the features selected
                                              by RFE (subset of the full list)
 
INTERNAL PIPELINE STEPS (stored inside "model"):
  1. Scaler   → RobustScaler or StandardScaler (or passthrough)
  2. Sampler  → SMOTE / RandomOverSampler / RandomUnderSampler (or passthrough)
  3. RFE      → Recursive Feature Elimination (LogisticRegression base estimator,
                C=0.01, liblinear solver); selects N features from the full list
  4. Classifier → Best classifier found by GridSearchCV (TabPFN)
  5. Calibration → Platt scaling (sigmoid) via CalibratedClassifierCV (cv=3)
 
  NOTE: All preprocessing (scaling, resampling, feature selection) is encapsulated
  inside the pipeline. You do NOT need to manually scale or select features before
  calling predict_proba(). Simply pass the full feature matrix.
 
================================================================================
REQUIRED INPUT FEATURES (full feature set — RFE selects the final subset)
================================================================================
 
  miRNA FEATURES (10 targets; column names must contain the patterns below):
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Pattern   Example column name        Notes
  ───────   ────────────────────────   ────────────────────────────────────────
  '187'     hsa_mir_187                Expression value as 2^(−ΔCt)
  '149'     hsa_mir_149                Expression value as 2^(−ΔCt)
  '205'     hsa_mir_205                Expression value as 2^(−ΔCt)
  '150'     hsa_mir_150                Expression value as 2^(−ΔCt)
  '143'     hsa_mir_143                Expression value as 2^(−ΔCt)
  '485'     hsa_mir_485                Expression value as 2^(−ΔCt)
  '200a'    hsa_mir_200a               Expression value as 2^(−ΔCt)
  '23a'     hsa_mir_23a                Expression value as 2^(−ΔCt)
  '106b'    hsa_mir_106b               Expression value as 2^(−ΔCt)
  '151a'    hsa_mir_151a               Expression value as 2^(−ΔCt)
 
  ⚠️  IMPORTANT — miRNA SCALE:
      The training data used raw 2^(−ΔCt) relative expression values.
      If your external cohort provides −ΔCt values (as stored in the INCA-OV
      dataset), apply the back-transformation BEFORE passing to the model:
          X[cols_mir] = 2 ** (−X[cols_mir])
      This step is performed explicitly in the EXTERNAL DATASET PREPARATION
      section of this script (see "X_rel_*" variables).
 
  CLINICAL FEATURES:
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Column name        Type      Description
  ────────────────   ───────   ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  age_at_index       float     Patient age at diagnosis (years)
  figo_stage         int       FIGO staging (1–4)
  MUC16              float     CA-125 serum level — ⚠️ must be log2-transformed
                               before passing to the model:
                                   MUC16 = log2(MUC16_raw + 1)
 
================================================================================
TARGET VARIABLE
================================================================================
 
  Column name : ClassProg
  Encoding    : Poor → 1  (event / poor prognosis)
                Good → 0  (no event / good prognosis)
 
